  "findings": [
    "The live worker and engine facade match delivered rc.2 bytes and have a JavaScript MIME type; no CSP response header was present in the inspected responses.",
    "Executable responses advertise Cache-Control public,max-age=604800; Cloudflare HIT was observed for the worker.",
    "Root HTML is modified by an injected Cloudflare analytics script, so exact rc.2 shell length/hash checks cannot pass.",
    "Explicit index.html and repair.html requests redirect to directories ending in 404; the first is independently sufficient to reject the old precache install."
  ],
  "inference": "A stale browser or CDN worker is consistent with the reported no-message bootstrap failure. The actual failure inside the user browser was not reproduced in the clean review browser, so this is not a confirmed per-browser root cause.",
  "resultingChanges": [
    "Release-specific executable asset directories and service-worker filename.",
    "Canonical offline shell embedded in service worker instead of fetching host-modified or redirected HTML.",
    "Recovery directory entry and HTTP-cache refresh in addition to scoped CacheStorage cleanup.",
    "Worker-ready handshake and bounded exact-response inspection on opaque bootstrap failures."
  ],
  "externalMutation": "None. The current hosted deployment was inspected and its example was run in the review browser; no server files or hosting settings were changed."
